From 428457c981222d34b50d426678b0d3b81733fa10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:24:06 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Withdraw the flow governor credit quanta

With credit that crosses the network no longer held, what was left held a server's download credit until 16 to 32 KiB had gathered. On the stand that saves no processor time: eight downloads cost 24.7 s per gigabyte on the server with it and 24.1 without under CUBIC, 25.1 and 24.8 under BBR.

Every piece of credit a reader returns goes on as it comes, in both directions and at both ends, as before the quanta. Holding upload credit did save about a tenth of the server's processor time on uploads, and under BBR it cost the next download nothing; under CUBIC it made that download start slower, which is why it went.
